WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:06.296
Choosing a private education is one of the biggest commitments a family makes. It isn't a single bill.

00:00:06.296 --> 00:00:13.165
It's a promise that runs for many years, alongside a mortgage, everyday life, and everything else you want for your family.

00:00:13.615 --> 00:00:15.749
John: We want the very best for Michael and May.

00:00:16.199 --> 00:00:18.417
Jane: And we want to be sure we can keep that promise.

00:00:18.867 --> 00:00:25.054
Meet John and Jane. Here's how Easy School Fees Planner helps families like theirs, in four simple steps.

00:00:26.554 --> 00:00:34.508
Step one, tell the planner about your family. Step two, add your schools. Step three, see how the fees are funded from your income and savings.

00:00:34.508 --> 00:00:37.455
And step four, plan your next home around those fees.

00:00:38.955 --> 00:00:49.345
Start with your family. Enter each parent's pay, and any time away from work, such as parental leave. The planner works out your take-home pay after income tax and the Medicare levy.

00:00:49.795 --> 00:00:57.453
Enter some basic details, such as the state you live in, each child's year of birth, and when they plan to start school. Names are optional.

00:00:57.903 --> 00:01:02.533
Jane: Michael starts Prep in 2027, and May follows in 2029.

00:01:04.033 --> 00:01:12.566
Next, add your schools. Enter the fees for each stage, primary and secondary, and the planner carries them forward using the yearly fee increase you choose.

00:01:13.016 --> 00:01:15.811
John: We're weighing up two different secondary schools for Michael.

00:01:16.261 --> 00:01:25.754
You can add up to three alternatives for each child, and compare what each one would cost your family over the whole plan. Scholarships and sibling discounts can be included too.

00:01:27.254 --> 00:01:35.505
Now for the important question. Where does the money come from? The planner pays living costs, housing and school fees from your take-home pay first.

00:01:35.505 --> 00:01:37.665
If there's a gap, your savings step in.

00:01:38.115 --> 00:01:43.597
Anything still missing is flagged as a shortfall, so you can see the tight years long before they arrive.

00:01:44.047 --> 00:01:47.311
Jane: Seeing the pressure points early is exactly what we needed.

00:01:48.811 --> 00:01:55.034
Then there's the house. Compare staying where you are with moving and buying a new house, or renting for a while first.

00:01:55.034 --> 00:02:00.054
For each option, the planner works out the deposit, the stamp duty, the loan and the repayments.

00:02:00.504 --> 00:02:06.904
A table shows what happens if you buy in each different year, so you can see when buying works best alongside the fees.

00:02:08.404 --> 00:02:17.577
The Interactive Planning Board brings everything together on one page, year by year. Drag the purchase to a different year. Stretch a rental. Move the school years.

00:02:17.577 --> 00:02:21.716
Add a work break, or a windfall, and watch every figure underneath update.

00:02:22.166 --> 00:02:24.427
John: Let's see what happens if we buy a year later.

00:02:24.877 --> 00:02:30.744
Because the whole plan is on one page, the trade-offs are clear, and you can try as many what-ifs as you like.

00:02:32.244 --> 00:02:39.442
And your information stays yours. When you save to the cloud, your plan is encrypted in your own browser, so no one else can read it.

00:02:39.442 --> 00:02:44.745
The built-in assistant answers questions about how the planner works, and never sees your numbers.

00:02:46.245 --> 00:02:54.181
The planner gives general information, not personal financial advice, so speak with a licensed professional before making big decisions.

00:02:54.631 --> 00:02:56.338
Jane: Now we can plan with confidence.

00:02:56.788 --> 00:02:59.391
John: For Michael, for May, and for the whole family.

00:02:59.841 --> 00:03:10.294
Plan wisely, to give your children the best head start. Sign up today, using your tablet or larger device, to start exploring the exciting possibilities ahead for you and your family.
